Topic 20 – Access Modifiers
Objective: Understand public, private, protected and default access across classes and packages.
No.	Program	Requirement
01	Public Access	Create a class with public variable and method. Access them from another class in the same package.
02	Private Access	Create a class with private variables and methods. Attempt access from another class and observe the restrictions.
03	Default Access	Create a class with default access members and access them from another class in the same package.
04	Protected Access	Create a parent class with protected members and access them from a child class in the same package.
05	Protected Cross-Package	Create a parent class in one package and child class in another package. Access protected members through inheritance.
06	Private Constructor	Create a class with a private constructor and demonstrate why an object cannot be created directly from another class.
07	Access Modifier Comparison	Create four variables using all four access modifiers and test access from another class in the same package.
08	Cross-Package Access	Create a class with public, protected, default and private methods. Access them from a class in another package.
09	Access Modifier in Inheritance	Create parent and child classes and demonstrate which members can be accessed through inheritance.
10	Framework Access Design	Design a class with private test data, protected reusable methods, public execution methods and default helper methods.